---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro'
import { analyticsEnabled, renderPrivacyAnalytics } from '@zyankov/design-system/render'

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Zyankov.eu'
const description = 'What Zyankov.eu processes: browser storage, anonymous analytics, shared links, embedded calculators and Google AdSense, and how to contact us.'
const jsonLd = {
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  dateModified: '2026-11-15',
}
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/" lang="en" alternates={{ en: '/privacy/', bg: '/bg/poveritelnost/' }} noAds={true} project="hub" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
      <p class="eyebrow">Your information</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: November 15, 2026</p>
      <p class="intro">
        This policy explains what information may be processed when you visit Zyankov.eu,
        including its calculators, articles, Letterwell and BuildCalc. It describes the current
        site setup; please check it again whenever a project or third-party service changes.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller for Zyankov.eu is Zlatko Yankov, based in Bulgaria. For privacy
          questions or requests, contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@zyankov.eu">hello@zyankov.eu</a>
          (also on the <a href="/about/#contact">About page</a>).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information processed when you visit</h2>
        <p>
          The hosting provider that serves these static pages may process technical request
          data such as your IP address, browser and device details, requested URL, and request
          time to deliver and secure the service. The site owner does not receive calculator
          inputs or word searches through an application backend. Hosting-provider logs are
          subject to the provider's own retention and privacy practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Fonts and images are served from zyankov.eu itself. Pages do not request fonts from
          Google Fonts or other font services.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site has no accounts and no first-party cookies. Calculators and word tools run in
          your browser; Letterwell searches a dictionary downloaded from this site, and the
          letters you enter are not sent to Zyankov.eu. The
          <a href="/blog/why-small-browser-tools/">reasons for building the tools this way</a> are
          explained in a short article.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Browser storage on your device</h2>
        <p>
          The site saves a few preferences and game states in your browser's local storage. They
          stay on your device and are not sent to the site owner. You can remove them by
          clearing this site's data in your browser settings. The keys are:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>zyankov-theme</code>: your light or dark theme, shared by all projects. Older keys <code>letterwell-theme</code> and <code>buildcalc-theme</code> are read once to carry an earlier choice over.</li>
          <li><code>buildcalc-units</code>: the measurement system (metric or US) chosen in BuildCalc.</li>
          <li><code>zyankov-recent</code>: the addresses of the last twelve tool pages you opened, for "Your tools" on the homepage (it is not filled on the homepage, the blog, embedded calculators or inside frames; the homepage has a button to clear it).</li>
          <li><code>zyankov-favourites</code>: the tools you starred on the homepage.</li>
          <li><code>zyankov-energy-list</code> and <code>zyankov-energy-list-bill</code>: the appliance list you build and the bill amount you enter in the energy cost calculators.</li>
          <li><code>zy-daily-game-v1</code>, <code>zy-daily-stats-v1</code>, <code>zy-daily-hints-v1</code> and <code>zy-daily-unlimited-v1</code> (English game: <code>zy-daily-en-…</code>): today's guesses, your statistics, the hints you opened and the practice game of the daily word game. The homepage reads the game and statistics keys to show your progress on its cards.</li>
          <li><code>zy-anagram-today-v1</code> and <code>zy-anagram-stats-v1</code> (English game: <code>zy-anagram-en-…</code>): today's progress and statistics of the daily anagram.</li>
          <li><code>letterwell-meanings</code>: whether word meanings are shown in the Wordle solver.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Letterwell also keeps up to five recent searches in temporary page memory so you can
          reuse them while the page remains open. This search history is not saved to local
          storage and is cleared when you leave or reload the page. The site does not use
          session storage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Share links</h2>
        <p>
          The "Share link", "Copy list" and similar buttons build an address that contains the
          values you entered (for example areas, prices, a date, an amount or a name you typed
          for a countdown) as parameters after the "?" in the URL. Anyone who has the link can
          see those values, and so can the messaging or email service you send it through. Pages
          you open from such a link fill the form from the URL, and the link is also visible to
          the hosting provider in its request logs. Share a link only if you are comfortable
          with that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Calculators embedded on other websites</h2>
        <p>
          Some calculators (the Bulgarian ones under <code>/bg/vgradi/</code>, and BuildCalc
          under <code>/calculators/embed/</code>) can be embedded in other websites. The
          embedded page is loaded from zyankov.eu, so the hosting provider and the analytics
          service below process the request as for any other page. The embedded page shows no
          site bar, footer or ad script. It records the embed events listed below, including
          the domain name of the page that embeds it (taken from the browser's referrer, when
          the browser sends one). Depending on your browser, embedded calculators may use the
          same browser storage as described above. The website that embeds a calculator is
          responsible for its own page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <Fragment set:html={renderPrivacyAnalytics('en')} />
        {analyticsEnabled && (
          <>
            <p>
              Besides page views, the site records these anonymous events. They carry only names
              and categories (such as the tool, the language or a count), never the letters,
              measurements or amounts you enter:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Word tools: searching for words, Wordle guesses and meaning lookups, crossword and Spelling Bee searches, and clicks on "try next" suggestions (with the language, the number of letters or results, and the guess number).</li>
              <li>Daily games: starting and finishing a puzzle (win or loss, number of guesses), opening hints, sharing a result, and solving, hinting or giving up the daily anagram.</li>
              <li>Calculators: running a calculation, copying a shopping list, opening a shared link (with the calculator and, in BuildCalc, the unit system), the energy calculator's appliance list, and copying a sum in words.</li>
              <li>Sharing: using a share or copy-link button, and which tool it was.</li>
              <li>Feedback: pressing "Yes, thanks" or "Not really" under a calculator result, or the "Write to us" link, with the calculator and the language. No text is collected: writing to us opens your own mail app.</li>
              <li>Homepage: adding or removing a favourite tool (the tool's id), switching the quick estimate, opening a daily game card, and clicks between projects in the top bar or footer.</li>
              <li>Embedded calculators: viewing, using and copying the embed code of an embedded calculator, with the calculator and the domain name of the embedding page.</li>
            </ul>
          </>
        )}
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Zyankov.eu is set up for Google AdSense. The AdSense script is included in the content
          pages of Zyankov.eu, Letterwell and BuildCalc. It is not included in this privacy
          policy, the terms of use, the disclaimer or the embedded calculators. The site's own
          code does not place any ad units on its pages; if Google shows ads through the script,
          Zyankov.eu does not control which ads appear. Zyankov.eu itself sets no advertising
          cookies.
        </p>
        <p>
          When the AdSense script is loaded, and when ads are shown, Google and its partners
          may process technical information such as your IP address and browser or device
          details, and may use cookies or similar technologies to serve, limit and measure ads
          and, where allowed, to personalise them. Those cookies belong to Google, not to
          Zyankov.eu, and the site owner cannot read them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where Google requires it (for example for visitors in the European Economic Area, the
          United Kingdom and Switzerland), Google's consent message asks for your choice before
          personalised advertising is used. You can change or withdraw your choice at any time with
          <button class="link-button" type="button" data-zy-consent>Privacy settings</button>,
          also linked in the footer of every page, except in calculators embedded on other websites.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can manage Google ad personalisation at
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noreferrer">adssettings.google.com</a>
          and read how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
        <p>
          You can control local storage through your browser settings. Depending on where you
          live, applicable data-protection laws may give you rights to request access,
          correction, deletion, restriction, or objection to certain processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a privacy question or request, contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@zyankov.eu">hello@zyankov.eu</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated when the site or its services change. The date at the top
          shows when it was most recently reviewed.
        </p>
      </section>
</PageLayout>
